1
00:00:05,714 --> 00:00:07,716
[pop song fades in]

2
00:00:09,635 --> 00:00:14,347
[singer]
<i>♪ Paint my wounds, lover ♪</i>

3
00:00:14,348 --> 00:00:15,641
[inhales]

4
00:00:15,766 --> 00:00:21,229
<i>♪ Make the pain... ♪</i>
[indistinct]

5
00:00:21,230 --> 00:00:24,149
[Yi-hsuan] <i>I should never have
met you.</i>

6
00:00:27,653 --> 00:00:30,989
<i>I shouldn't have come to you.</i>

7
00:00:31,114 --> 00:00:35,368
[singer]
<i>♪ Make it nice and fine... ♪</i>

8
00:00:35,369 --> 00:00:38,746
[Yi-hsuan] <i>It's you
who turned me into this...</i>

9
00:00:38,747 --> 00:00:41,375
[thunder rumbling]

10
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:43,835
<i>...a life of total chaos.</i>

11
00:00:46,713 --> 00:00:52,677
[singer] <i>♪ Come and taste
the...</i> [indistinct] ♪

12
00:00:52,678 --> 00:00:55,180
<i>♪ My flesh ♪</i>

13
00:00:58,100 --> 00:00:59,351
[Yi-hsuan] <i>Between us,</i>

14
00:01:00,519 --> 00:01:03,522
<i>from the very first night
we met,</i>

15
00:01:04,773 --> 00:01:06,608
<i>it was a mistake.</i>

16
00:01:07,276 --> 00:01:13,240
[singer]
<i>♪ Don't you wanna come, right? ♪</i>

17
00:01:14,074 --> 00:01:16,827
[Yi-hsuan] <i>No one can decide
how it begins,</i>

18
00:01:18,078 --> 00:01:22,165
<i>but I can decide how it ends.</i>

19
00:01:22,624 --> 00:01:28,630
[singer] <i>♪ Say, you'll never
treat me nice ♪</i>

20
00:01:29,298 --> 00:01:31,633
[Yi-hsuan] <i>For everything
we created together,</i>

21
00:01:35,178 --> 00:01:37,180
<i>for the person
most important to me,</i>

22
00:01:39,766 --> 00:01:42,102
<i>whatever it takes...</i>

23
00:01:43,312 --> 00:01:45,105
[singer]
<i>♪ Get to the heart of it ♪</i>

24
00:01:45,230 --> 00:01:46,898
<i>♪ Get to the dark of it ♪</i>

25
00:01:47,107 --> 00:01:48,858
<i>♪ Get to the heart of it ♪</i>

26
00:01:48,859 --> 00:01:50,902
<i>♪ Get to the dark of it ♪</i>

27
00:01:51,111 --> 00:01:52,778
<i>♪ Get to the heart of it ♪</i>

28
00:01:52,779 --> 00:01:55,282
<i>♪ Get to the dark of it
Get... ♪</i>

29
00:01:55,407 --> 00:01:56,616
[Yi-hsuan] <i>I will...</i>

30
00:01:56,617 --> 00:01:58,577
[singer]
<i>♪ Get to the dark of it ♪</i>

31
00:02:00,245 --> 00:02:01,538
[Yi-hsuan] <i>...destroy you.</i>

32
00:02:03,332 --> 00:02:06,877
[singer] <i>♪ Someday, you can
find sunshine, sunshine ♪</i>

33
00:02:07,127 --> 00:02:10,505
[singing in Mandarin]

34
00:02:11,798 --> 00:02:13,799
<i>♪ Come, come to hope ♪</i>

35
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,927
<i>♪ Hope, hope, don't go ♪</i>

36
00:02:16,178 --> 00:02:18,262
<i>♪ I believe in you someday ♪</i>

37
00:02:18,263 --> 00:02:20,390
[singing in Mandarin]

38
00:02:29,274 --> 00:02:31,276
- [pen writing]
- [paper crumpling]

39
00:02:33,362 --> 00:02:36,365
[quirky music playing]

40
00:02:38,158 --> 00:02:39,785
[shutter clicking]

41
00:02:43,330 --> 00:02:46,333
[Yi-hsuan] <i>Why are the noodles
and sauce separate? Failed.</i>

42
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:53,131
<i>Even with penne,
the sauce isn't clinging to it.</i>

43
00:02:53,256 --> 00:02:54,341
<i>Failed.</i>

44
00:02:55,926 --> 00:02:59,470
<i>Squid-ink pasta only goes
with seafood, not meat sauce.</i>

45
00:02:59,471 --> 00:03:02,682
<i>You don't even know
your basics, and you invite me
to a taste test?</i>

46
00:03:02,683 --> 00:03:05,351
<i>- You're wasting my time.</i>
- [gulp]

47
00:03:05,352 --> 00:03:06,478
GOURMET, MEGA INFLUENCER,

48
00:03:06,603 --> 00:03:08,479
SCATHING FOOD CRITIC
CHAO YI-HSUAN

49
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:10,982
[Yi-hsuan] <i>When people meet me,
they're usually surprised
by two things.</i>

50
00:03:11,191 --> 00:03:13,985
<i>First, how can I know so much
about food, love to eat,
and dare to eat anything?</i>

51
00:03:14,236 --> 00:03:15,903
<i>Every dish, every flavor,
you name it.</i>

52
00:03:15,904 --> 00:03:17,656
<i>It's like I've got a radar
in my mouth or something.</i>

53
00:03:18,281 --> 00:03:21,159
<i>Yup. That's my superpower,
built-in since day one.</i>

54
00:03:21,284 --> 00:03:25,330
<i>Second, why am I so smart
and athletic at the same time?</i>

55
00:03:25,455 --> 00:03:28,792
<i>The one who keeps asking me
that is my college bestie,
Chang Chien-wu.</i>

56
00:03:28,917 --> 00:03:31,460
<i>He says I'm basically an alien.</i>

57
00:03:31,461 --> 00:03:35,506
<i>And he's not wrong.
Because I hold the stars
in my hands.</i>

58
00:03:35,507 --> 00:03:37,843
<i>I'm a food influencer
with over a million followers.</i>

59
00:03:37,968 --> 00:03:39,885
<i>I'm brutally honest,
no sugarcoating.</i>

60
00:03:39,886 --> 00:03:41,972
<i>Regular folks call me
the Queen.</i>

61
00:03:42,222 --> 00:03:44,015
<i>Good food is
whatever I declare it to be.</i>

62
00:03:44,266 --> 00:03:46,851
<i>Whether it's five stars,
three stars, or even just one,</i>

63
00:03:46,852 --> 00:03:48,728
<i>my word can make
or break a place.</i>

64
00:03:48,729 --> 00:03:50,521
WASTING MY TIME

65
00:03:50,522 --> 00:03:53,858
[Yi-hsuan] <i>Some places have
no talent and zero effort.</i>

66
00:03:53,859 --> 00:03:57,069
<i>You really dared to put
something this awful
on a plate?</i>

67
00:03:57,070 --> 00:03:58,029
<i>Total garbage.</i>

68
00:03:59,448 --> 00:04:01,365
<i>This world has never been fair.</i>

69
00:04:01,366 --> 00:04:03,994
<i>Some people are destined
for success.
Some are destined to fail.</i>

70
00:04:04,244 --> 00:04:06,204
<i>And me?
I freaking hate failures.</i>

71
00:04:06,329 --> 00:04:07,747
Get up!

72
00:04:07,748 --> 00:04:10,541
I'm sorry for asking you
to come to the school,
Mrs. Chao.

73
00:04:10,542 --> 00:04:13,586
- Is Yi-hsuan not doing well
at school?
- She's a brilliant girl.

74
00:04:13,587 --> 00:04:16,047
But I'm worried
she's too strict with herself.

75
00:04:16,298 --> 00:04:17,423
She's overly competitive.

76
00:04:17,424 --> 00:04:18,717
[ball thudding]

77
00:04:20,844 --> 00:04:22,762
[Tina] <i>She has been like this
since she was little.</i>

78
00:04:22,763 --> 00:04:25,389
But I don't see it as a problem.

79
00:04:25,390 --> 00:04:28,392
But she can't seem
to accept any failure.

80
00:04:28,393 --> 00:04:30,937
Sometimes,
it gets quite extreme.

81
00:04:33,899 --> 00:04:35,901
You can't even take a ball
at this speed?

82
00:04:36,610 --> 00:04:38,945
Dive for it!
What are your kneepads for?

83
00:04:39,070 --> 00:04:41,489
[teacher]
<i>We lost the inter-class
volleyball competition</i>

84
00:04:41,490 --> 00:04:43,575
<i>because a teammate
missed a ball.</i>

85
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:46,578
<i>Yi-hsuan forced him
to practice with her.</i>

86
00:04:46,703 --> 00:04:48,747
<i>Now, he refuses to come
to gym class.</i>

87
00:04:49,372 --> 00:04:52,417
Again... Again!

88
00:04:54,002 --> 00:04:55,295
Get up!

89
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:57,756
That's enough.
We've done this 300 times.

90
00:04:57,881 --> 00:04:59,382
You're not tired, but I am!

91
00:05:00,008 --> 00:05:01,551
I'm not tired?

92
00:05:04,596 --> 00:05:05,514
Look.

93
00:05:05,972 --> 00:05:08,933
For you,
I've almost ruined my hand.

94
00:05:08,934 --> 00:05:10,936
And you're telling me
I'm not tired?

95
00:05:11,061 --> 00:05:14,396
Honestly, I think being able
to accept some failures

96
00:05:14,397 --> 00:05:16,024
is something Yi-hsuan
needs to learn.

97
00:05:18,944 --> 00:05:20,987
[Tina] <i>What is success to you?</i>

98
00:05:21,112 --> 00:05:22,781
Am I successful?

99
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:25,075
No, you're not.

100
00:05:25,367 --> 00:05:28,661
A restaurant needs to be big
to be successful.

101
00:05:28,662 --> 00:05:29,913
[sighs]

102
00:05:30,455 --> 00:05:32,374
So, I'm a loser?

103
00:05:32,833 --> 00:05:34,793
It's okay if you're a loser.

104
00:05:34,918 --> 00:05:36,086
I will be a success.

105
00:05:37,671 --> 00:05:39,673
[ambient chatter]

106
00:05:44,761 --> 00:05:46,680
[energetic music playing]

107
00:05:48,682 --> 00:05:51,851
<i>Whatever I eat
becomes a part of me.</i>

108
00:05:51,852 --> 00:05:57,023
<i>So I hate, I really hate
being forced to lie
that something is good.</i>

109
00:05:57,148 --> 00:05:59,776
<i>Forcing me to say it
is like murdering me.</i>

110
00:06:00,861 --> 00:06:01,862
<i>Just like this.</i>

111
00:06:05,991 --> 00:06:08,368
[camera clicking]

112
00:06:17,377 --> 00:06:18,836
[camera clicking]

113
00:06:18,837 --> 00:06:22,591
[quirky music playing]

114
00:06:31,391 --> 00:06:33,726
<i>This restaurant's
white wine clam pasta?</i>

115
00:06:33,727 --> 00:06:36,937
<i>The sauce hasn't
been emulsified
with the pasta at all.</i>

116
00:06:36,938 --> 00:06:38,898
<i>The sauce and spaghetti
are fully separated.</i>

117
00:06:38,899 --> 00:06:40,358
<i>Am I eating soup noodles?</i>

118
00:06:40,483 --> 00:06:43,235
<i>And they claim to be
a true pasta restaurant.</i>

119
00:06:43,236 --> 00:06:44,154
<i>What a joke!</i>

120
00:06:47,699 --> 00:06:48,909
Give me back my phone.

121
00:06:49,618 --> 00:06:51,912
- [manager]
Will you delete it or not?
- I have freedom of speech.

122
00:06:52,037 --> 00:06:55,081
I invited you to eat here.
It's fine if you don't
like the food.

123
00:06:55,206 --> 00:06:58,751
- Did you have to post that?
- You snuck photos of me first.

124
00:06:58,752 --> 00:07:00,879
Isn't that forcing
my recommendation?

125
00:07:01,713 --> 00:07:03,757
I didn't want
to say anything at first,
but since you made this awkward,

126
00:07:03,882 --> 00:07:06,801
don't blame me
for telling the truth.
Give it back!

127
00:07:08,178 --> 00:07:11,513
Yi-hsuan,
we were high school classmates.
It doesn't have to be like this.

128
00:07:11,514 --> 00:07:13,933
Because we were classmates,
I've been very polite.

129
00:07:13,934 --> 00:07:15,018
Polite?

130
00:07:15,810 --> 00:07:17,228
[scoffs]

131
00:07:17,479 --> 00:07:19,773
You can't leave
without deleting the video.
That's it!

132
00:07:27,739 --> 00:07:29,156
Fine.

133
00:07:29,157 --> 00:07:31,743
I'll delete my video.
You'll delete yours too. Okay?

134
00:07:35,455 --> 00:07:39,124
Think about it.
Which one will hurt you more?

135
00:07:39,125 --> 00:07:41,252
My negative reviews, right?

136
00:07:42,087 --> 00:07:45,674
So, we'll both delete them.
Then it's fair. Okay?

137
00:07:50,762 --> 00:07:51,846
Okay.

138
00:07:53,807 --> 00:07:55,808
Listen, guys.
Their food is bad.

139
00:07:55,809 --> 00:07:57,810
And they confiscate your phone,
so you can't post a bad review.

140
00:07:57,811 --> 00:07:59,813
What are you doing?
Stop filming! You...

141
00:07:59,938 --> 00:08:01,940
- You're in the video.
- You're going too far!

142
00:08:03,525 --> 00:08:05,609
- [yelps]
- [Lu-yung] Hey, hey, hey!

143
00:08:05,610 --> 00:08:08,488
No need to get violent!
Can't you just talk nicely?

144
00:08:12,117 --> 00:08:15,619
Who the hell are you?
Some social justice warrior?

145
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:17,163
Do you even know what happened?

146
00:08:17,288 --> 00:08:18,623
Let go!

147
00:08:20,959 --> 00:08:22,585
- [yelps]
- [Lu-yung] Hey!

148
00:08:23,545 --> 00:08:24,629
What's wrong with you?

149
00:08:27,257 --> 00:08:28,133
Hey!

150
00:08:28,967 --> 00:08:30,635
You didn't have to slap her.

151
00:08:35,557 --> 00:08:37,809
Do you know how much
she scammed from my dad?

152
00:08:41,062 --> 00:08:43,856
Do you know how it feels
to have your family ruined?

153
00:08:43,857 --> 00:08:45,233
[dramatic music playing]

154
00:08:48,695 --> 00:08:49,738
You don't.

155
00:08:50,947 --> 00:08:52,949
Because you know nothing.

156
00:08:55,493 --> 00:08:56,411
I'm sorry.

157
00:09:03,877 --> 00:09:04,753
Idiot!

158
00:09:06,963 --> 00:09:09,007
[quirky music playing]

159
00:09:14,262 --> 00:09:15,722
[car horn blares]

160
00:09:15,847 --> 00:09:16,972
[camera clicks]

161
00:09:16,973 --> 00:09:18,223
[Chien-wu] Look!

162
00:09:18,224 --> 00:09:20,934
I got the Queen for a taste-test
at Jin Lai Xuan.

163
00:09:20,935 --> 00:09:23,021
She used to be my classmate.
Not bad, right?

164
00:09:23,146 --> 00:09:25,648
She's really great.

165
00:09:26,816 --> 00:09:29,027
No wonder Hsiu-wen
always says you're good.

166
00:09:29,152 --> 00:09:30,028
Really?

167
00:09:31,654 --> 00:09:32,863
Yes.

168
00:09:32,864 --> 00:09:34,699
And she asked
if you're free tomorrow night.

169
00:09:34,824 --> 00:09:36,658
She wants to go out with you.

170
00:09:36,659 --> 00:09:39,953
She'll make herself smell good,
and after dinner,
she'll bring you home

171
00:09:39,954 --> 00:09:41,873
- to see her cat doing backflips.
- Leave me alone.

172
00:09:41,998 --> 00:09:44,166
That's enough, all of you.

173
00:09:44,167 --> 00:09:46,752
If you're not on the next shift,
get out of here.

174
00:09:46,753 --> 00:09:48,922
- Do you want overtime?
- [clerk] No, thanks.

175
00:09:49,798 --> 00:09:50,715
Hey.

176
00:09:51,216 --> 00:09:54,677
You'll see your dad
at the launch later, right?

177
00:09:55,261 --> 00:09:56,179
Yeah.

178
00:09:57,097 --> 00:09:58,223
Talk to him for me.

179
00:10:01,184 --> 00:10:02,935
- Okay.
- Okay?

180
00:10:02,936 --> 00:10:06,231
- I'll find a chance.
- Come on.
We all really need a raise.

181
00:10:07,065 --> 00:10:08,608
- Bye.
- Bye.

182
00:10:09,234 --> 00:10:10,734
[phone vibrating]

183
00:10:10,735 --> 00:10:12,612
HSIU-WEN

184
00:10:14,322 --> 00:10:15,782
- Hello?
- [Hsiu-wen] <i>Chien-wu.</i>

185
00:10:15,907 --> 00:10:17,366
<i>Are you sure
your friend's coming?</i>

186
00:10:17,367 --> 00:10:18,910
<i>She hasn't replied
to me at all.</i>

187
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:21,286
She hasn't replied to you?

188
00:10:21,287 --> 00:10:24,081
[Hsiu-wen] <i>No. But I've got
everything ready
for her tasting.</i>

189
00:10:24,082 --> 00:10:25,250
<i>Can you get in touch with her?</i>

190
00:10:25,375 --> 00:10:27,252
Okay, I'm on it. Bye.

191
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:33,633
<i>The sauce hasn't
been emulsified
with the pasta at all.</i>

192
00:10:34,759 --> 00:10:35,760
[sighs]

193
00:10:49,357 --> 00:10:51,401
I QUIT

194
00:10:51,651 --> 00:10:54,237
- [ball thudding]
- [indistinct chatter]

195
00:11:14,966 --> 00:11:15,925
You okay?

196
00:11:18,803 --> 00:11:19,971
[Yi-hsuan screams]

197
00:11:22,348 --> 00:11:23,974
We're late. We have to go.

198
00:11:23,975 --> 00:11:24,893
I'm not going!

199
00:11:25,810 --> 00:11:28,771
If I have to praise Chang Xin,
I'm not going.

200
00:11:29,147 --> 00:11:30,315
No, you don't have to.

201
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:32,150
Just say whatever you want.
Be my guest.

202
00:11:32,275 --> 00:11:35,820
Everyone says that,
but can't take it
when I tell the truth.

203
00:11:38,364 --> 00:11:39,324
I won't go.

204
00:11:39,449 --> 00:11:42,160
You restaurant people
piss me off.

205
00:11:42,285 --> 00:11:43,786
You don't respect me.

206
00:11:45,705 --> 00:11:48,373
Please, Yi-hsuan. I'll be dead
if you don't go. It's true.

207
00:11:48,374 --> 00:11:49,375
Give it back!

208
00:11:52,253 --> 00:11:53,254
[sighs]

209
00:12:00,386 --> 00:12:03,181
Let me hit you with the ball,
and I'll go.

210
00:12:05,725 --> 00:12:07,060
- Hit where?
- Your face.

211
00:12:07,852 --> 00:12:09,145
Right in your face.

212
00:12:11,147 --> 00:12:14,150
[quirky music playing]

213
00:12:25,119 --> 00:12:26,704
Are you an idiot?

214
00:12:26,829 --> 00:12:29,874
How could you take
those online rants seriously?

215
00:12:31,167 --> 00:12:33,877
You told your followers.
I thought that it was true.

216
00:12:33,878 --> 00:12:36,714
It was true then,
but that doesn't mean
it'll stay true.

217
00:12:36,839 --> 00:12:38,382
Don't you have
to explain it to them?

218
00:12:38,383 --> 00:12:40,133
No. They understand.

219
00:12:40,134 --> 00:12:43,096
I'm emotional.
That's why they love me.

220
00:12:44,097 --> 00:12:44,973
Let's go.

221
00:12:48,309 --> 00:12:51,312
[upbeat music playing]

222
00:12:57,277 --> 00:12:59,279
[bird calls]

223
00:13:00,863 --> 00:13:03,449
[Yi-hsuan]
<i>I don't believe in fate.
I believe more in chances.</i>

224
00:13:06,869 --> 00:13:08,954
<i>When I'm aiming at those birds,</i>

225
00:13:08,955 --> 00:13:13,209
<i>the probability that
they'll die is 0.00001%.</i>

226
00:13:14,794 --> 00:13:17,797
[upbeat music playing]

227
00:13:29,017 --> 00:13:32,102
[Yi-hsuan]
<i>But as long
as the probability isn't zero,</i>

228
00:13:32,103 --> 00:13:33,938
<i>anything can happen.</i>

229
00:13:34,397 --> 00:13:36,190
[Lu-yung]
Delicious Taiwanese dishes!

230
00:13:36,816 --> 00:13:38,525
Check in and get a free gift!

231
00:13:38,526 --> 00:13:40,110
[imitates chicken call]

232
00:13:40,111 --> 00:13:41,946
10% off!

233
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:43,906
15% off when you check in!

234
00:13:47,535 --> 00:13:49,412
[singer]
<i>♪ Come, come to hope ♪</i>

235
00:13:49,537 --> 00:13:51,789
<i>♪ Hope, hope, don't go ♪</i>

236
00:13:51,914 --> 00:13:53,999
<i>♪ I believe in you someday ♪</i>

237
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:56,127
[singing in Mandarin]

238
00:14:15,021 --> 00:14:16,396
[both gasping]

239
00:14:16,397 --> 00:14:18,065
Watch out! Someone's ahead!

240
00:14:18,066 --> 00:14:20,193
- [tires screeching]
- Another one!

241
00:14:20,318 --> 00:14:21,485
[grunting]

242
00:14:21,486 --> 00:14:23,029
[screams]

243
00:14:27,658 --> 00:14:31,370
[Yi-hsuan] Chang Chien-wu!

244
00:14:31,371 --> 00:14:34,082
[screaming]

245
00:14:40,630 --> 00:14:44,050
[slowed down] Oh, no!

246
00:14:46,511 --> 00:14:49,222
[singer] <i>♪ Don't you dare
Waste another minute... ♪</i>

247
00:14:49,347 --> 00:14:53,266
[Lu-yung] <i>I thought
a probability of 0.00001%</i>

248
00:14:53,267 --> 00:14:55,394
<i>was low enough.</i>

249
00:14:55,395 --> 00:15:00,233
[slowed down] It's you again.

250
00:15:00,358 --> 00:15:02,526
[Lu-yung]
<i>But somehow, in one day,</i>

251
00:15:02,527 --> 00:15:05,571
<i>I run into
the same chicken twice.</i>

252
00:15:06,447 --> 00:15:09,616
[singer]
<i>♪ Before I turn over then go ♪</i>

253
00:15:09,617 --> 00:15:11,576
<i>♪ I pray that... ♪</i>

254
00:15:11,577 --> 00:15:14,330
[Lu-yung] <i>That's a chance
so low it defies logic.</i>

255
00:15:15,248 --> 00:15:17,375
<i>If it's not fate
playing tricks,</i>

256
00:15:19,335 --> 00:15:24,506
<i>then it's just me
being incredibly unlucky.</i>

257
00:15:24,507 --> 00:15:27,552
[singer]
<i>♪ There's no one above me ♪</i>

258
00:15:28,719 --> 00:15:30,263
<i>♪ Just highly... ♪</i>

259
00:15:30,388 --> 00:15:31,931
[song screeches to halt]

260
00:15:32,056 --> 00:15:33,516
[groans]

261
00:15:41,732 --> 00:15:43,943
You... Aren't you...

262
00:15:45,153 --> 00:15:46,486
[Chien-wu] Chao Yi-hsuan!

263
00:15:46,487 --> 00:15:47,613
Chao Yi-hsuan!

264
00:15:47,738 --> 00:15:49,115
Are you alright?

265
00:15:51,242 --> 00:15:52,118
You okay?

266
00:15:53,995 --> 00:15:55,037
[grunts]

267
00:15:55,413 --> 00:15:56,289
[grunts]

268
00:15:56,414 --> 00:15:58,082
You'll kill me sooner or later!

269
00:15:59,167 --> 00:16:00,543
I'm so sorry.

270
00:16:02,753 --> 00:16:03,754
Sir?

271
00:16:05,047 --> 00:16:05,882
Are you alright?

272
00:16:07,258 --> 00:16:08,718
It's dangerous riding like that.

273
00:16:10,011 --> 00:16:11,345
I'm so sorry.

274
00:16:11,721 --> 00:16:13,055
Ride safely from now on.

275
00:16:13,931 --> 00:16:14,765
[Chien-wu] Okay.

276
00:16:16,017 --> 00:16:17,143
Are you sure you're okay?

277
00:16:17,768 --> 00:16:18,603
Yeah.

278
00:16:24,650 --> 00:16:27,653
[soft dramatic music playing]

279
00:16:35,036 --> 00:16:37,038
[frying pan sizzling]

280
00:16:47,298 --> 00:16:48,132
[Lu-yung] Dad?

281
00:16:49,258 --> 00:16:51,301
[cart wheel rattling]

282
00:16:51,302 --> 00:16:52,678
[ambient hospital noise]

283
00:16:54,639 --> 00:16:55,473
[Chien-wu] You're awake.

284
00:16:57,058 --> 00:16:58,142
Feeling better?

285
00:17:04,732 --> 00:17:07,150
Don't worry.
The doctor said you're unharmed.

286
00:17:07,151 --> 00:17:09,070
You passed out
mostly because of fatigue.

287
00:17:10,363 --> 00:17:11,405
But you're...

288
00:17:13,199 --> 00:17:14,242
Are you looking for something?

289
00:17:15,618 --> 00:17:18,246
Have you...
Have you seen my mascot suit?

290
00:17:18,663 --> 00:17:22,041
- You mean this?
- Yeah. It has a body suit.

291
00:17:23,376 --> 00:17:27,129
It's... The body was cut up
by the medical staff.

292
00:17:34,095 --> 00:17:36,847
I'll also pay for this.
And all the medical bills.

293
00:17:38,432 --> 00:17:39,433
I'm really sorry.

294
00:17:41,769 --> 00:17:43,521
[Lu-yung]
I'm busy. I've got to go.

295
00:17:43,646 --> 00:17:44,689
[Chien-wu] Are you sure?

296
00:17:45,856 --> 00:17:46,816
[Lu-yung] Yeah.

297
00:17:50,111 --> 00:17:51,153
[Chien-wu] Hey, man.

298
00:17:51,696 --> 00:17:53,405
I still need
your contact details.

299
00:17:53,406 --> 00:17:56,158
[indistinct chatter]

300
00:18:03,249 --> 00:18:04,208
[Chien-wu] Sorry.

301
00:18:06,210 --> 00:18:07,586
[Lu-yung]
If you're really sorry,

302
00:18:07,587 --> 00:18:09,714
come to my restaurant
with your friends.

303
00:18:11,716 --> 00:18:14,259
JIN LAI HAO - GRAND OPENING

304
00:18:14,260 --> 00:18:15,719
- Okay.
- Why are people still using

305
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:17,554
mascots and fliers these days?

306
00:18:17,555 --> 00:18:19,557
[quirky music playing]

307
00:18:22,184 --> 00:18:24,603
- Do you think it's useless?
- Useless.

308
00:18:24,604 --> 00:18:26,314
You won't get any new customers.

309
00:18:28,816 --> 00:18:30,526
How do I get new customers then?

310
00:18:31,527 --> 00:18:33,738
Everyone's using
the internet now.

311
00:18:33,863 --> 00:18:34,780
I know.

312
00:18:35,573 --> 00:18:37,741
But without popularity
and enough followers,

313
00:18:37,742 --> 00:18:38,909
there's no reach.

314
00:18:51,714 --> 00:18:53,799
The photos are ugly
and the captions are too long.

315
00:18:54,550 --> 00:18:55,926
Are you writing a diary?

316
00:18:56,761 --> 00:18:59,764
Only your mom's interested
in your diary.

317
00:18:59,889 --> 00:19:02,475
Posts are loaded with hashtags,

318
00:19:02,600 --> 00:19:05,436
stressing the food's good,
fresh with the best ingredients.

319
00:19:05,561 --> 00:19:06,854
They're basically all nonsense.

320
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:10,316
If you don't position yourself,
how are people
going to find you?

321
00:19:10,441 --> 00:19:12,818
Why should they dine
at your restaurant?

322
00:19:14,612 --> 00:19:15,779
[scoffs]

323
00:19:15,780 --> 00:19:17,657
Because my food is good.

324
00:19:18,491 --> 00:19:21,451
That might be a fact,
but facts don't interest people.

325
00:19:21,452 --> 00:19:23,245
Branding does.

326
00:19:29,168 --> 00:19:30,920
What do you think
my restaurant lacks?

327
00:19:32,546 --> 00:19:33,464
One month.

328
00:19:34,590 --> 00:19:36,175
If your restaurant
still opens in one month,

329
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:38,468
I'll eat there
to celebrate my graduation.

330
00:19:38,469 --> 00:19:40,346
Then maybe
I'll answer your question.

331
00:19:42,765 --> 00:19:43,808
See you in a month.

332
00:19:52,483 --> 00:19:54,484
He looked honest and sincere.

333
00:19:54,485 --> 00:19:56,862
A guy his age, still so naive.

334
00:20:01,909 --> 00:20:02,827
Hello?

335
00:20:04,995 --> 00:20:06,539
Yes, I've dealt with everything.

336
00:20:06,664 --> 00:20:09,582
But we won't make it today.
I'm sorry.

337
00:20:09,583 --> 00:20:11,585
Because my food is good.

338
00:20:12,253 --> 00:20:13,462
See you in a month.

339
00:20:14,630 --> 00:20:18,300
[Chien-wu] Yes, luckily a guy
saved my friend.
Otherwise, we'd be in trouble.

340
00:20:19,635 --> 00:20:21,220
Alright, bye.

341
00:20:21,345 --> 00:20:22,638
Come on. I'll take you home.

342
00:20:23,347 --> 00:20:25,766
How can such a lame restaurant
still open in a month?

343
00:20:36,277 --> 00:20:38,738
[dramatic music playing]

344
00:20:52,793 --> 00:20:54,879
[Lu-yung]
<i>Five-Color Egg Yolk Shrimp.
It's not on the menu.</i>

345
00:20:55,004 --> 00:20:57,923
<i>Because it's complicated
to make,
most places don't serve it.</i>

346
00:20:59,008 --> 00:21:01,051
<i>But today, a customer
specifically asked for it.</i>

347
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:03,888
<i>No matter what they order,
I'll make it happen.</i>

348
00:21:04,889 --> 00:21:06,515
<i>We won't disappoint
any customers.</i>

349
00:21:10,936 --> 00:21:11,979
<i>I'm Chou Lu-yung.</i>

350
00:21:12,646 --> 00:21:14,564
<i>This restaurant
is called Jin Lai Hao.</i>

351
00:21:14,565 --> 00:21:16,734
<i>Jin Lai was my dad's name.</i>

352
00:21:17,401 --> 00:21:20,571
<i>I want this name to live on
along with the flavors
he passed down.</i>

353
00:21:23,282 --> 00:21:24,783
<i>First, fry the filling
at a low heat</i>

354
00:21:24,784 --> 00:21:26,285
<i>around 150 degrees Celsius
to cook it through.</i>

355
00:21:26,410 --> 00:21:28,078
<i>Then crank up the heat
to 220 degrees</i>

356
00:21:28,329 --> 00:21:29,996
<i>and fry for about ten seconds
to get it nice and crispy.</i>

357
00:21:29,997 --> 00:21:32,750
<i>When you eat the shrimp,
it should be
around 45 to 50 degrees.</i>

358
00:21:33,334 --> 00:21:35,586
<i>That's the perfect temperature
to bring out
its sweetest flavor.</i>

359
00:21:39,089 --> 00:21:42,092
Here's your Five-Color
Egg Yolk Shrimp.

360
00:21:44,428 --> 00:21:45,638
[customer] Let me try it first.

361
00:21:49,725 --> 00:21:52,644
[Lu-yung] <i>If this can bring back
some good memories for them,</i>

362
00:21:52,645 --> 00:21:53,896
<i>and leave them wanting more,</i>

363
00:21:54,730 --> 00:21:55,731
<i>then I'll know</i>

364
00:21:56,524 --> 00:21:57,566
<i>I did it right.</i>

365
00:21:58,317 --> 00:22:00,694
[upbeat music playing]

366
00:22:05,449 --> 00:22:07,117
[Lu-yung] <i>Yu-li and Chin-nan
are my partners.</i>

367
00:22:07,368 --> 00:22:09,328
<i>We get up every day at 4:25,</i>

368
00:22:09,453 --> 00:22:10,913
<i>and head to the market to pick
the freshest ingredients.</i>

369
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:14,291
<i>Then it's back to
the restaurant, make the broth,
prepare the sauces,</i>

370
00:22:14,416 --> 00:22:17,044
<i>clean up, and prep everything.
Everything's ready.</i>

371
00:22:17,711 --> 00:22:19,839
<i>All that's left is waiting for
the customers to walk in.</i>

372
00:22:20,756 --> 00:22:23,008
<i>Every dish we make
is our absolute best,</i>

373
00:22:23,133 --> 00:22:24,552
<i>to honor my dad's spirit.</i>

374
00:22:25,094 --> 00:22:26,929
<i>Start with the end in mind,
hold on to your beliefs.</i>

375
00:22:29,765 --> 00:22:30,933
[alarm beeps]

376
00:22:31,725 --> 00:22:33,977
<i>A full stomach makes
a lousy chef.</i>

377
00:22:33,978 --> 00:22:36,522
<i>Hunger sharpens your senses</i>

378
00:22:37,982 --> 00:22:39,567
<i>and makes you want
something badly.</i>

379
00:22:41,443 --> 00:22:44,780
<i>Until the day we meet.</i>

380
00:22:48,450 --> 00:22:49,785
JIN LAI HAO

381
00:22:57,626 --> 00:22:58,585
Welcome.

382
00:22:58,586 --> 00:23:00,045
- Welcome.
- Welcome.

383
00:23:01,797 --> 00:23:03,590
Excuse me.
Can I use the restroom?

384
00:23:03,591 --> 00:23:05,009
[song screeches to halt]

385
00:23:09,763 --> 00:23:11,765
- [dance music playing]
- [cheering]

386
00:23:17,396 --> 00:23:19,148
[yells]

387
00:23:19,398 --> 00:23:20,691
[party crowd chanting]

388
00:23:21,775 --> 00:23:22,902
[indistinct]

389
00:23:25,029 --> 00:23:26,906
[cheering]

390
00:23:27,823 --> 00:23:30,492
[classmate 1]
Chao Yi-hsuan! Happy graduation!

391
00:23:30,868 --> 00:23:32,453
[classmate 2] Happy graduation!

392
00:23:32,953 --> 00:23:36,039
Hey! Let's keep the party
going tonight.

393
00:23:36,040 --> 00:23:37,875
I know a place with great food.

394
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:39,877
There's a restaurant
I want to go.

395
00:23:40,002 --> 00:23:40,878
Which one?

396
00:23:41,837 --> 00:23:43,464
Not sure if it's still open.

397
00:23:46,717 --> 00:23:48,010
[groans]

398
00:23:51,138 --> 00:23:53,140
[muttering]

399
00:23:54,642 --> 00:23:56,894
[Chin-nan]
The cabbages are all rotten.

400
00:24:05,027 --> 00:24:07,154
I'll clean out
these rotten ones.

401
00:24:11,825 --> 00:24:12,701
[Lu-yung] Go ahead.

402
00:24:14,662 --> 00:24:16,955
You're ditching Five Willow Fish
and Eight-Treasure Meatballs?

403
00:24:16,956 --> 00:24:18,082
They're really good though.

404
00:24:19,750 --> 00:24:21,877
I have to.
Nobody's ordered them.

405
00:24:28,217 --> 00:24:29,551
[sighs]

406
00:24:31,720 --> 00:24:33,597
I don't think anybody
is going to come now.

407
00:24:33,722 --> 00:24:35,599
I'll go look around
at other places.

408
00:24:41,689 --> 00:24:43,691
[soft jazz playing]

409
00:24:45,943 --> 00:24:48,570
Order some food, at least.

410
00:24:48,988 --> 00:24:51,573
You'll have gastric issues,
drinking like that.

411
00:24:53,909 --> 00:24:55,661
[bar chatter]

412
00:24:55,786 --> 00:24:57,913
[laughs]

413
00:24:58,956 --> 00:25:00,290
Chao Yi-hsuan!

414
00:25:01,250 --> 00:25:02,626
Uncle Wen?

415
00:25:02,918 --> 00:25:04,669
Wait for me upstairs.

416
00:25:04,670 --> 00:25:06,045
[classmate] Okay.

417
00:25:06,046 --> 00:25:07,965
- Hello.
- I heard
it's your graduation day.

418
00:25:08,090 --> 00:25:09,133
Yeah.

419
00:25:12,177 --> 00:25:13,178
Thank you.

420
00:25:15,180 --> 00:25:17,016
What are your plans?

421
00:25:17,891 --> 00:25:19,101
I'll go work for you.

422
00:25:19,810 --> 00:25:21,686
Mom tells me
you come here a lot.

423
00:25:21,687 --> 00:25:23,981
You're either super rich
or want to date her.

424
00:25:25,149 --> 00:25:27,568
I'm super poor.
That's why I'm not dating her.

425
00:25:30,654 --> 00:25:32,990
Your world is complicated.
I don't get it.

426
00:25:34,825 --> 00:25:37,119
Among those boys,
which one is your boyfriend?

427
00:25:37,661 --> 00:25:39,162
None of them.

428
00:25:39,163 --> 00:25:41,998
I'm leaving.
We're going to grab a bite.

429
00:25:41,999 --> 00:25:43,876
Don't drink too much. Bye, Mom.

430
00:25:44,835 --> 00:25:45,794
Bye.

431
00:25:50,758 --> 00:25:52,176
She grew up
in the blink of an eye.

432
00:25:53,343 --> 00:25:55,845
Every time I see her,

433
00:25:55,846 --> 00:25:58,182
I'm glad I didn't complete
my mission back then.

434
00:26:01,685 --> 00:26:04,229
[soft tense music playing]

435
00:26:14,073 --> 00:26:15,115
[Tina] Here.

436
00:26:16,575 --> 00:26:18,077
This one is on me.

437
00:26:22,331 --> 00:26:24,291
Thank you
for bringing me Yi-hsuan.

438
00:26:33,884 --> 00:26:35,052
This is it?

439
00:26:35,844 --> 00:26:36,887
JIN LAI HAO

440
00:26:37,012 --> 00:26:38,097
I think they're closed.

441
00:26:38,722 --> 00:26:40,098
This place looks so run-down!

442
00:26:40,099 --> 00:26:42,225
Graduation is all about
eating something awesome.

443
00:26:42,226 --> 00:26:44,977
Listen, my friend's family
runs a bistro.

444
00:26:44,978 --> 00:26:47,773
- The food is awesome.
- Don't come in
if you don't want to.

445
00:26:49,691 --> 00:26:51,276
Whoa! Oh.

446
00:26:54,738 --> 00:26:56,782
- [bell rings]
- [laughs and chatter]

447
00:27:02,246 --> 00:27:03,413
Dining in?

448
00:27:03,622 --> 00:27:04,747
[Chien-wu] Table for four.

449
00:27:04,748 --> 00:27:07,333
[Chin-nan]
Okay. Have a seat. This way.

450
00:27:07,334 --> 00:27:08,335
[classmate 1] Thank you.

451
00:27:11,046 --> 00:27:12,422
They have lobsters.

452
00:27:12,631 --> 00:27:14,841
[classmate 2] Not bad.
But the vibe's off.

453
00:27:14,842 --> 00:27:16,927
Let's order the good stuff.

454
00:27:17,970 --> 00:27:19,805
We'll have both
lobsters and crabs.

455
00:27:19,930 --> 00:27:21,931
Lobsters, sea urchins, crabs.
Let's have them all.

456
00:27:21,932 --> 00:27:24,059
And... awesome!

457
00:27:24,977 --> 00:27:26,310
Lobster, grouper...

458
00:27:26,311 --> 00:27:28,021
Let's take a look at the menu.

459
00:27:28,772 --> 00:27:29,939
Okay, okay.

460
00:27:29,940 --> 00:27:31,108
[quirky music playing]

461
00:27:31,233 --> 00:27:32,818
Thanks!

462
00:27:32,943 --> 00:27:34,986
If I miss these dishes...

463
00:27:34,987 --> 00:27:36,113
Chin-nan.

464
00:27:38,907 --> 00:27:40,826
Isn't that...

465
00:27:40,951 --> 00:27:43,120
that girl... the popular...

466
00:27:43,871 --> 00:27:45,788
food influencer?

467
00:27:45,789 --> 00:27:47,708
Excuse me. Lower your voices.

468
00:27:50,127 --> 00:27:53,797
It's getting late.
Our neighbors will complain.

469
00:27:54,715 --> 00:27:55,883
Sorry.

470
00:27:57,384 --> 00:27:58,302
Who?

471
00:27:59,303 --> 00:28:01,180
That girl is
the "Queen of Reviews."

472
00:28:01,305 --> 00:28:03,307
Let's make sure we do our best,

473
00:28:03,432 --> 00:28:05,309
and serve her properly.

474
00:28:05,976 --> 00:28:09,188
If she likes our restaurant,
maybe we'll go viral.

475
00:28:09,313 --> 00:28:10,981
Viral, you know?

476
00:28:12,816 --> 00:28:13,859
No problem.

477
00:28:17,362 --> 00:28:20,490
Excuse me. Have you guys
decided on your order?

478
00:28:20,741 --> 00:28:21,700
What else?

479
00:28:22,367 --> 00:28:24,411
- [Chien-wu]
Stir-fried Pork Liver.
- [Chin-nan] Okay.

480
00:28:30,334 --> 00:28:31,877
[classmate 1] Cheers!

481
00:28:32,502 --> 00:28:33,503
Here. Pork Liver.

482
00:28:36,006 --> 00:28:37,799
- We'd like to order some more.
- Okay.

483
00:28:37,925 --> 00:28:39,509
We want the braised eggplant,
scrambled eggs with onion,

484
00:28:39,760 --> 00:28:40,719
and Hakka stir-fry.

485
00:28:41,345 --> 00:28:43,347
Sorry, could you repeat that?

486
00:28:45,849 --> 00:28:49,061
We want braised eggplant,
scrambled eggs with onion,

487
00:28:49,186 --> 00:28:51,021
and Hakka stir-fry.

488
00:28:51,146 --> 00:28:52,814
Do you have 18 Days Draft Beer?

489
00:28:56,860 --> 00:28:58,028
It's fine.

490
00:28:58,153 --> 00:28:59,905
We'll have Gold Medal.
Gold Medal is fine.

491
00:29:00,030 --> 00:29:01,072
Yeah, that's fine.

492
00:29:01,073 --> 00:29:02,074
Gold Medal is okay.

493
00:29:02,199 --> 00:29:03,950
I want 18 Days too.

494
00:29:03,951 --> 00:29:05,369
[classmate 2]
Me too. Let's have a six-pack.

495
00:29:05,494 --> 00:29:07,370
- I want it too.
- [classmate 1] Not enough.
Two six-packs.

496
00:29:07,371 --> 00:29:09,247
- [Chien-wu] Too many for us.
- [classmate 1]
Let's have two six-packs.

497
00:29:09,248 --> 00:29:10,498
[Chien-wu] Don't waste it.

498
00:29:10,499 --> 00:29:12,375
- No, the two of us
can finish it.
- Or...

499
00:29:12,376 --> 00:29:14,211
A bottle of red wine first,
on us.

500
00:29:14,336 --> 00:29:17,047
We're out of 18 Days.
We'll go get some now.

501
00:29:18,423 --> 00:29:21,718
- [classmate 1] Fine. Hurry up.
- Not bad, eh? Red wine.

502
00:29:21,843 --> 00:29:23,135
[classmate 2]
A bottle of red wine!

503
00:29:23,136 --> 00:29:24,428
It's too much. Can we finish it?

504
00:29:24,429 --> 00:29:25,889
- 18 Days?
- Yeah.

505
00:29:26,014 --> 00:29:28,016
How could we go
get draft beer now?

506
00:29:28,517 --> 00:29:30,727
Didn't you say
we'd serve that influencer well?

507
00:29:30,852 --> 00:29:31,936
I'll buy some.

508
00:29:31,937 --> 00:29:33,479
Wait. I'm afraid
I can't handle all this.

509
00:29:33,480 --> 00:29:36,441
I need to make
three more dishes.
What if they order more?

510
00:29:37,484 --> 00:29:38,442
Maybe...

511
00:29:38,443 --> 00:29:41,237
you ask Lu-yung to buy them.

512
00:29:41,238 --> 00:29:44,366
- Yeah. I'll call him.
- Okay.

513
00:30:03,885 --> 00:30:05,262
[bell rings]

514
00:30:08,015 --> 00:30:09,766
So? How is it?

515
00:30:09,891 --> 00:30:10,892
Here's yours.

516
00:30:12,811 --> 00:30:14,271
Listen to me.

517
00:30:14,396 --> 00:30:16,773
That girl is
a social media influencer
with a sharp tongue.

518
00:30:16,898 --> 00:30:18,608
The point is that she's popular
with plenty of followers.

519
00:30:18,817 --> 00:30:20,277
If she posts something
saying she loves us,

520
00:30:20,402 --> 00:30:21,944
our popularity will skyrocket.

521
00:30:21,945 --> 00:30:23,447
So this fried rice
you're making,

522
00:30:23,572 --> 00:30:24,947
you gotta give it
your whole heart.

523
00:30:24,948 --> 00:30:26,950
[soft upbeat music playing]

524
00:30:32,205 --> 00:30:33,457
Here goes.

525
00:31:00,942 --> 00:31:02,944
[music intensifies]

526
00:31:31,515 --> 00:31:32,891
[Lu-yung] Fried rice is ready!

527
00:31:33,975 --> 00:31:35,977
[overlapping chatter]

528
00:31:37,396 --> 00:31:39,397
Why are you guys still on this?

529
00:31:39,398 --> 00:31:40,690
- United Kingdom.
- Come on.

530
00:31:40,899 --> 00:31:42,233
The UK rocks.

531
00:31:42,234 --> 00:31:43,860
You afraid I don't know
you're studying abroad?

532
00:31:43,985 --> 00:31:46,238
Listen. The UK is amazing.

533
00:31:47,531 --> 00:31:49,533
- I'm so sorry. I'm so sorry.
- Go to hell!

534
00:31:50,325 --> 00:31:53,954
What the hell?
What lousy customer service!

535
00:31:55,497 --> 00:31:58,041
- I'm so sorry.
- What the hell? Damn!

536
00:31:59,126 --> 00:32:00,001
Hey!

537
00:32:05,382 --> 00:32:06,675
I didn't mean it.

538
00:32:10,303 --> 00:32:11,555
I'm really sorry.

539
00:32:16,518 --> 00:32:18,978
What a total buzzkill!

540
00:32:18,979 --> 00:32:20,604
We're just trying
to have a meal.

541
00:32:20,605 --> 00:32:22,231
I don't know what you're doing.

542
00:32:22,232 --> 00:32:23,400
What do you want?

543
00:32:27,404 --> 00:32:29,906
What? What did I do?

544
00:32:30,031 --> 00:32:31,574
What's your problem?

545
00:32:31,575 --> 00:32:33,618
- What's your problem?
- Come on.

546
00:32:34,453 --> 00:32:37,121
I'm sorry. It's our fault.
Please forgive us.

547
00:32:37,122 --> 00:32:40,082
And... please lower your voices.

548
00:32:40,083 --> 00:32:41,418
The neighbors will complain.

549
00:32:41,543 --> 00:32:43,586
I'm not loud.

550
00:32:43,587 --> 00:32:44,963
Am I loud?

551
00:32:45,088 --> 00:32:48,174
So this is how you treat
your customers?

552
00:32:48,175 --> 00:32:49,425
No. I'm sorry.

553
00:32:49,426 --> 00:32:51,761
Is this how you treat
a pretty girl?

554
00:32:52,596 --> 00:32:55,557
- What?
Do I need to act like you?
- That's enough!

555
00:32:56,725 --> 00:32:58,435
Aren't you embarrassed?

556
00:32:58,935 --> 00:32:59,769
Damn!

557
00:33:03,482 --> 00:33:04,524
Let's go, Chien-wu.

558
00:33:05,650 --> 00:33:06,776
So annoying.

559
00:33:07,986 --> 00:33:09,154
Did I say you can leave?

560
00:33:09,279 --> 00:33:10,571
- What?
- Let go!

561
00:33:10,572 --> 00:33:11,781
- Let go!
- I haven't finished my drink.

562
00:33:12,032 --> 00:33:13,283
Where are you going?

563
00:33:14,284 --> 00:33:16,536
- What are you doing, Yi-hsuan?
- It hurts!

564
00:33:17,621 --> 00:33:19,122
Damn! You bitch!

565
00:33:23,293 --> 00:33:25,045
Apologize to my staff
and the girl.

566
00:33:26,505 --> 00:33:28,048
Why should I?

567
00:33:30,133 --> 00:33:31,092
We have security cameras.

568
00:33:31,510 --> 00:33:32,511
Hit me.

569
00:33:32,636 --> 00:33:33,803
It's proof
that I don't fight back.

570
00:33:39,726 --> 00:33:40,810
You think I won't?

571
00:33:41,019 --> 00:33:42,145
Damn! You bastard!

572
00:33:42,270 --> 00:33:43,187
Damn!

573
00:33:43,188 --> 00:33:45,064
[energetic music playing]

574
00:33:45,065 --> 00:33:46,107
Damn!

575
00:33:46,816 --> 00:33:48,235
What the hell?

576
00:33:49,110 --> 00:33:50,111
Chin-nan!

577
00:33:53,782 --> 00:33:54,658
Damn!

578
00:34:00,789 --> 00:34:02,332
Chin-nan?

579
00:34:02,457 --> 00:34:04,543
Chin-nan? Are you alright?

580
00:34:06,503 --> 00:34:07,671
It hurts.

581
00:34:07,796 --> 00:34:09,339
[officer] What's going on?

582
00:34:09,464 --> 00:34:11,841
Police! Who's the owner?

583
00:34:12,592 --> 00:34:15,387
Someone reported you
for being too noisy.
It's noise pollution.

584
00:34:17,347 --> 00:34:19,307
And it looks like
there was a fight here.

585
00:34:21,101 --> 00:34:22,227
Anyone involved, come with me.

586
00:34:22,727 --> 00:34:23,853
I'm the owner.

587
00:34:24,813 --> 00:34:26,189
I'll go with you.

588
00:34:28,400 --> 00:34:31,027
- I'm the one who hit him.
I'll go.
- [officer] Shut up!

589
00:34:31,152 --> 00:34:32,445
If you were fighting,
you're coming in.

590
00:34:40,453 --> 00:34:41,830
[camera clicks]

591
00:34:49,588 --> 00:34:52,132
Excuse me.
Are you leaving
a negative review?

592
00:34:53,550 --> 00:34:54,384
No.

593
00:34:58,305 --> 00:35:01,307
This is also partially
our fault.

594
00:35:01,308 --> 00:35:03,768
Don't worry
about the compensation.

595
00:35:13,194 --> 00:35:15,488
You still have
a sausage fried rice.

596
00:35:16,281 --> 00:35:17,407
Will you take it to go?

597
00:35:45,602 --> 00:35:48,605
[soft dramatic music playing]

598
00:36:08,958 --> 00:36:11,961
Did the owner make this?

599
00:36:13,505 --> 00:36:14,381
Yes.

600
00:36:21,888 --> 00:36:23,973
[mother]
My son has been beaten up.

601
00:36:24,182 --> 00:36:26,810
So, I want at least
100,000 dollars.

602
00:36:27,727 --> 00:36:29,353
Are they lobsters?

603
00:36:29,354 --> 00:36:30,980
That's too much. Do you want
to see the surveillance footage?

604
00:36:31,231 --> 00:36:32,649
- Shut up!
- Damn!

605
00:36:33,817 --> 00:36:34,984
What are you doing?

606
00:36:36,319 --> 00:36:37,903
- [mother] See?
- [Lu-yung] Enough!

607
00:36:37,904 --> 00:36:39,489
- Son of a bitch!
- Chin-nan!

608
00:36:46,830 --> 00:36:48,623
It's our fault.
Go for a medical examination.

609
00:36:49,290 --> 00:36:50,667
We'll pay
a reasonable compensation.

610
00:36:50,792 --> 00:36:51,876
Chang Chien-wu.

611
00:36:52,585 --> 00:36:54,462
Your dear brother is here.

612
00:36:55,213 --> 00:36:56,381
What trouble are you in now?

613
00:36:57,507 --> 00:36:58,757
Why are you here?

614
00:36:58,758 --> 00:37:00,802
[dramatic music playing]

615
00:37:03,513 --> 00:37:05,432
Damn. Am I seeing things?

616
00:37:07,267 --> 00:37:08,476
Chou Lu-yung?

617
00:37:09,269 --> 00:37:10,395
Hey, mate.

618
00:37:11,563 --> 00:37:13,857
- What?
- You know him?

619
00:37:14,482 --> 00:37:16,775
Yeah,
he's my high school classmate.

620
00:37:16,776 --> 00:37:18,862
It was only for a day though.

621
00:37:22,323 --> 00:37:23,366
What's the situation?

622
00:37:24,617 --> 00:37:26,995
I've finished my statement.
They're talking
about the compensation.

623
00:37:28,580 --> 00:37:29,539
Need my help?

624
00:37:36,796 --> 00:37:39,340
The old lady
wants 100,000 dollars.
You can pay it if you want.

625
00:37:40,383 --> 00:37:41,885
Fine. We'll see.

626
00:37:45,013 --> 00:37:47,681
Officer? I can go
after my statement, right?

627
00:37:47,682 --> 00:37:48,558
[officer] Yes.

628
00:37:50,977 --> 00:37:53,813
This is my business card.
You can contact me
about the compensation.

629
00:37:56,649 --> 00:37:57,901
Come back after your statement.

630
00:38:11,539 --> 00:38:12,415
[Chien-yuan] Hey!

631
00:38:14,417 --> 00:38:15,960
Wait for me, man.

632
00:38:17,086 --> 00:38:18,296
Hey.

633
00:38:18,922 --> 00:38:19,798
Chou Lu-yung!

634
00:38:25,428 --> 00:38:26,638
What do you want?

635
00:38:28,056 --> 00:38:30,642
I mean,
I haven't seen you for a while.

636
00:38:30,767 --> 00:38:32,602
Let's chat and catch up.

637
00:38:34,062 --> 00:38:35,605
There's nothing to talk about.

638
00:38:36,940 --> 00:38:39,442
I really want to help you.

639
00:38:39,567 --> 00:38:41,652
It's got to be hard for you
to earn money now.

640
00:38:41,653 --> 00:38:42,821
Why won't you let me help you?

641
00:38:44,864 --> 00:38:45,740
No.

642
00:38:47,992 --> 00:38:49,869
You haven't changed at all.

643
00:38:53,623 --> 00:38:55,499
Do you still think
I killed your dad?

644
00:38:55,500 --> 00:38:57,544
[dramatic music playing]

645
00:38:57,877 --> 00:38:58,837
What did you say?

646
00:39:02,549 --> 00:39:04,467
You heard it. Your dad.

647
00:39:13,643 --> 00:39:14,811
Yes.

648
00:39:14,936 --> 00:39:16,688
I did kill your dad.

649
00:39:17,564 --> 00:39:19,315
And I think he deserved it.

650
00:39:19,440 --> 00:39:20,732
[music intensifies]

651
00:39:20,733 --> 00:39:23,403
If he had listened to me,
he wouldn't have died.

652
00:39:24,779 --> 00:39:26,029
If he didn't die,

653
00:39:26,030 --> 00:39:27,615
you wouldn't have been in jail.

654
00:39:29,742 --> 00:39:32,870
So, you see?

655
00:39:32,871 --> 00:39:35,999
The one who put you
in this pathetic life is not me,

656
00:39:39,002 --> 00:39:40,461
but your dad.

657
00:39:53,766 --> 00:39:55,768
[credits music playing]
